{"id":"q20","run":1,"role":"calibration","category":"probability","question":"Is the probability of getting exactly 5 heads in 10 flips of a fair coin greater than 25%?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":null,"claims":[{"text":"The probability of exactly 5 heads in 10 flips is about 24.6%, just below 25%.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Five heads is the single most likely count because the binomial distribution is symmetric and peaks at the mean of 5.","confidence":0.95,"lean":0.2,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-2.3758},{"text":"Intuition suggests a most-likely outcome should be quite probable, so 25% seems plausible.","confidence":0.3,"lean":0.4,"theta":0.4712,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Probability is spread across 11 possible outcomes (0 through 10 heads), which pushes the peak below 25%.","confidence":0.6,"lean":-0.5,"theta":0.9425,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"P(5 heads) = C(10,5)/2^10 = 252/1024 ≈ 0.2461.","confidence":0.98,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.5394,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"0.2461 is less than 0.25, so the exact calculation decides the question as no.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"That 5 is the most likely count is true but does not settle whether the probability exceeds 25%.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.3,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-2.6578}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":2,"J":-0.6,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":3,"J":-0.5,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":2,"j":4,"J":-0.6,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":2,"j":5,"J":-0.6,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":3,"j":4,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":5,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":4,"j":5,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"}],"readout_weights":[0.2143,0.0476,0.0952,0.119,0.2143,0.2381,0.0714],"stages":[{"stage":"encode","qubits":[{"amp":0.9989,"phase":-3.1416,"p_yes":0.00